.TH V32AS-CONTROL 3 "2026-11-09" "v32as 20261109-dev" "Vircon32 assembler manual"
.SH NAME
IF, ELSE, ENDIF, WHILE, ENDWHILE \- structured control flow macros for v32as (lib/control.inc)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B %include "control.inc"
.sp
.BI "IF " "reg"
    ...
.B ELSE
    ...
.B ENDIF
.sp
.BI "WHILE " "reg"
    ...
.B ENDWHILE
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I lib/control.inc
provides structured
.B IF
/
.B ELSE
/
.B ENDIF
and
.B WHILE
/
.B ENDWHILE
on top of the
.B jf
and
.B jmp
instructions.
They are written with the extended preprocessor (contexts and private labels),
so they cannot be used with
.BR "v32as \-\-standard" .
Use them with
.B \-I lib
and include the file:
.PP
.nf
.RS
v32as \-I lib game.asm
.RE
.fi
.PP
.nf
.RS
%include "control.inc"
.RE
.fi
.PP
The file starts with
.BR %includeonce .
Macro names are case\-sensitive: they are written in capitals.
.PP
The condition is a CPU register, and the test is only whether it is zero or not;
a comparison has to be computed into a register first (for example with
.BR ieq ,
.BR ilt
or
.BR igt ).
The macros open a
.B %push
context whose private labels
.RB ( %$else ,
.BR %$end ,
.BR %$top )
are different every time, so the constructs nest.
The labels are named
.BR __C\fIn\fP_else ,
.B __C\fIn\fP_end
and
.BR __C\fIn\fP_top .
.SH MACROS
.TP
.BI "IF " "reg"
Run the following block when
.I reg
is not zero.
Expands to
.BI "jf " "reg" ", else-label" \fR.
.TP
.B ELSE
Optional.
Ends the block of the
.B IF
and starts the block that runs when the register was zero
(a
.B jmp
to the end, then the else label).
Only allowed after an
.BR IF .
.TP
.B ENDIF
Ends an
.B IF
or an
.B IF
\&...
.BR ELSE .
.TP
.BI "WHILE " "reg"
Repeat the following block as long as
.I reg
is not zero.
The test is made before each pass; the block must change the register or leave
the loop some other way.
.TP
.B ENDWHILE
Ends a
.BR WHILE :
a
.B jmp
back to the test.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.RS
%include "control.inc"
    IF R1
        mov R2, 1
    ELSE
        mov R2, 2
    ENDIF
    WHILE R3
        isub R3, 1
    ENDWHILE
.RE
.fi
.PP
expands (as shown by
.BR "v32as \-E \-P" )
to
.PP
.nf
.RS
    jf    R1, __C1_else
        mov R2, 1
    jmp   __C1_end
__C1_else:
        mov R2, 2
__C1_end:
__C2_top:
    jf    R3, __C2_end
        isub R3, 1
    jmp   __C2_top
__C2_end:
.RE
.fi
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.TP
.B IF: the condition must be a register
The argument of
.B IF
is not a CPU register.
.TP
.B WHILE: the condition must be a register
The argument of
.B WHILE
is not a CPU register.
.TP
.B ELSE without a matching IF
.TP
.B ENDIF without a matching IF
.TP
.B ENDWHILE without a matching WHILE
A construct was closed that is not the innermost open one.
.TP
.B unterminated %push context
An
.B IF
or
.B WHILE
was never closed before the end of the program.
.PP
Errors from inside a macro are reported at the line of the invocation, with a
note naming the macro.
A mismatched construct may also produce a follow\-on message from the macro's
own label.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR v32as (1),
.BR v32as\-inc (3),
.BR v32as\-language (7)
